<Cell ss:StyleID="data"><Data ss:Type="String">1 INDICATIONS AND USAGE Dextromethorphan hydrobromide and quinidine sulfate capsules are indicated for the treatment of pseudobulbar affect (PBA). PBA occurs secondary to a variety of otherwise unrelated neurologic conditions, and is characterized by involuntary, sudden, and frequent episodes of laughing and/or crying. PBA episodes typically occur out of proportion or incongruent to the underlying emotional state. PBA is a specific condition, distinct from other types of emotional lability that ...</Data></Cell>
